                <pb facs="0059" n="37" xml:id="pg37"/>

                <head>14. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On February 24, Wolf Ladejinsky wrote a
                    7-page letter to Walt Rostow covering the
                    political and economic situations in light of the Communist threat. He
                    concluded, “everything must be brought into play to insure the survival of
                    Vietnam.” (Kennedy Library, President’s Office File, Staff Memoranda, Rostow)</p>
            </div>
